@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<article class="privacy-policy">
    <h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>

    <h2>About this service</h2>
    <p>After the Credits is an independent movie discovery and recommendation demo.
        It helps you choose films based on your preferences and find viewing options in Ireland.
        You can use the website without registering or providing your name or email address.</p>

    <h2>Visitor sessions and cookies</h2>
    <p>When you first visit, the application creates a random visitor identifier and stores a protected version
        of it in an essential cookie.
        The cookie links your browser to your own movie records in the server database.
        It is HTTP-only and marked Secure in production. It expires 24 hours after the session is created.
        Returning visits do not extend that period.
        ASP.NET Core also uses an anti-forgery cookie to protect forms against unauthorized submissions.</p>
    <p>You can manage or remove cookies in your browser. Removing the visitor cookie prevents the website from
        recognizing that session and does not immediately delete its server-side records.</p>

    <h2>Information we store and how we use it</h2>
    <p>For each visitor session, the application stores the random identifier, creation and expiry times,
        onboarding progress (including skipped starter movie batches), movie IDs, Watchlist entries,
        watched status and personal ratings.
        These records are stored in a SQLite database on the server and are used to maintain your personal movie
        collection, exclude watched films and personalize recommendations.
        Movie choices may also be used to determine which genres to explore in a Wild Card recommendation.</p>
    <p>Search terms are sent to the movie information provider to return results.
        The application does not include advertising or analytics tracking integrations.
        Operational logs may record request details, movie-related diagnostics and calculated genre summaries.</p>

    <h2>Retention, deletion and Reset Demo</h2>
    <p>Your demo session is valid for 24 hours. Expired sessions and their associated movie records are deleted
        when the application subsequently processes a page request that runs its expiry cleanup.
        Consequently, removal from the active database may take place after the session expires.</p>
    <p>To remove your saved movie data sooner, use <strong>Reset Demo</strong> in the navigation while your session
        is active. This deletes the current visitor session and its associated movie records and removes its
        visitor cookie. Returning to the homepage starts a new session.
        You can also remove individual films from My Movies.</p>
    <p>The database contains a shared cache of numerical embeddings generated from public movie information.
        The cache is not connected to a particular visitor identifier and is not deleted by Reset Demo.
        Hosting and third-party logs, as well as any hosting backups, are subject to their own retention and
        deletion arrangements. Reset Demo does not erase those records.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>TMDB (The Movie Database).</strong> The application sends movie IDs, search queries and
            discovery filters to TMDB to obtain film information and viewing availability.
            Posters are loaded directly from TMDB's image service, which may receive browser and network
            information when a poster is requested.
            See <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/privacy-policy">TMDB's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>JustWatch.</strong> Viewing availability is provided by JustWatch through TMDB.
            The application queries TMDB for this data and does not make direct JustWatch API requests.
            If you follow a JustWatch link, you visit a separate service.
            See <a href="https://www.justwatch.com/ie">JustWatch</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Gemini API.</strong> Public movie titles, genres and plot summaries are sent to Gemini
            to generate embeddings. The application does not include your visitor identifier, cookie, personal
            rating or search text in the embedding request. Gemini may process the content and technical
            request information under the applicable service terms.
            See the <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/terms">Gemini API terms</a> and
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Railway.</strong> The application and its database are hosted on Railway.
            In providing hosting, Railway may process stored application data and request information, including
            IP addresses, browser user-agent information, request paths and timestamps.
            Hosting and operational logs may be retained separately from the 24-hour demo session and data may
            be processed outside Ireland or the European Economic Area.
            See <a href="https://railway.com/legal/privacy">Railway's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Privacy questions and requests</h2>
    <p>For questions about this policy or requests to access, correct or delete information, contact the
        project operator at <a href="mailto:tingtingnothere@gmail.com">tingtingnothere@gmail.com</a>.
        Because sessions use a random identifier, it may be difficult to locate a record after the visitor
        cookie is removed or has expired. Please do not send your cookie value or other sensitive information
        by email.</p>
    <p>Where applicable data protection law gives you further rights, you may also request restriction,
        object to processing or request portability. You may lodge a complaint with the relevant data
        protection authority. In Ireland, this is the
        <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie/">Data Protection Commission</a>.</p>
</article>
